<version>1.0.0</version>
<language>Rust</language>
Output src/character.rs. std only, f64. Modified Bessel functions of the first kind, integer order: bessel_i(n:u32, x:f64)->f64 for 0 <= x <= 200 with relative error below 1e-13: power series for x <= 2 n + 20 summed until terms fall below 1e-17 of the sum, otherwise Miller's backward recurrence normalized by I_0 from the series or asymptotic expansion; scaled variant bessel_i_scaled = exp(-x) I_n(x) to avoid overflow. SU(2) character expansion of the Wilson weight exp(beta a0(U)) = sum_j c_j(beta) chi_j(U), j = 0, 1/2, 1, ..., with c_j = (2j+1) 2 I_{2j+1}(beta)/beta; normalized coefficients u_j = c_j/((2j+1) c_0) = I_{2j+1}(beta)/I_1(beta). Exact 2D results on a periodic torus with V plaquettes (genus 1, each link in two plaquettes): Z = sum_j (c_j/(2j+1))^V; plaquette average <a0(U_p)> = (1/V) d/dbeta log Z, evaluated in scaled form, summing j until terms are below 1e-18 relative; infinite-volume limit I_2(beta)/I_1(beta). Wilson loop of area A in infinite volume u_{1/2}^A. Independent tests: tests/character.rs: Bessel values against reference digits for (n,x) in {0,1,2,5}x{0.5,1,2,10,50}; Wronskian-type identity I_{n-1} - I_{n+1} = (2n/x) I_n; small-beta limit <a0> -> beta/4; torus result converges to I_2/I_1 as V grows.
